#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Home Folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Two office locations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "Address"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Account disabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Password Management</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Password Management</guilabel> tab will appear if you have "
"shadow passwords, or any other similar things such as <filename>/etc/master."
"passwd</filename> in <acronym>BSD</acronym> flavor Unices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum number of days between password changes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of days after which a password expires if it hasn't been changed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of days before expiration the user will be warned"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether and when an account will be disabled if the password expires"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "A set date when the account expires"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Class</guilabel> (on <acronym>BSD</acronym> systems)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The date of the last password change is displayed near the top of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Groups</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Groups</guilabel> tab contains all the information about the "
"selected user's participation in groups. The primary group to which the user "
"belongs is set with the <guilabel>Set as Primary</guilabel> button. The user "
"can be assigned to additional groups by checking them in the large box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Group Properties</guilabel> dialog contains a list of all "
"users. Check the boxes for each user to be assigned to the selected group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding, Editing and Deleting Users or Groups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a user or group to the system, either choose <guimenuitem>Add</"
"guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>User</guimenu> or <guimenu>Group</guimenu> "
"menu, or click the relevant <guiicon>Add</guiicon> button on the toolbar. "
"The selected user or group can also be edited or deleted in the same way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customizing &kuser;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit user creation defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit the user creation defaults you can use the <guilabel>Connection</"
"guilabel> tab on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> page of &kuser;'s "
"configuration dialog, which is accessible via the menu "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kuser;</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. There you may change the defaults that are used "
"when creating a new user: Shell and Home Folder (or home folders volume). "
"You can choose whether to make a home folder on <quote>create</quote> or "
"not, and to copy a skeleton (standard configuration files) to the home "
"folder or not. You can also enable <guilabel>User private group</guilabel> "
"mechanism, which creates a new personal group with the creation of a new "
"user, and removes the personal group when the user is removed."
msgstr ""

